subproblem.statement:
Let n ∈ ℕ, D : ℝ → ℝ, E, G : ℝ → [0, ∞] and R, K, C ∈ ℝ with R > 0. Assume:
(a) for every ε > 0, E(s) ≤ ofReal(ε)·G(s) for all sufficiently small s > 0 (∀ᶠ s in 𝓝[>] 0);
(b) G(s) ≤ ofReal(C·sⁿ) for all sufficiently small s > 0;
(c) ‖D(r)‖ₑ ≤ ofReal((rⁿ)⁻¹)·ofReal(K)·E(R·r) for all sufficiently small r > 0.
Then D(r) → 0 as r → 0⁺, i.e. Tendsto D (𝓝[>] 0) (𝓝 0). No sign condition on K or C is assumed.

